<figure class="essay-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lapita-pottery.jpg" alt="Lapita pottery" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Lapita pottery was made by hand, without a wheel, and decorated before firing by pressing toothed tools into the damp clay to make lines of tiny dots, built into bands of geometric motifs and stylised human faces, with white lime rubbed into the impressions so that the patterns stood out against a red-slipped surface. <span class="essay-credit">Image: Torbenbrinker · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PortVilaLapita.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></span></figcaption></figure>
